el: null                    # LLM model for review (null = default)\n    max_iterations: 3              # Max review-modify cycles\n```\n\nAvailable steps for confirmation:\n- `propose` - After task analysis and proposal\n- `design` - After technical design\n- `implement` - After implementation\n- `verify` - After verification\n- `commit` - Before creating git commit\n\nReviewer modes:\n- `human` - Creates review request, waits for human approval\n- `llm` - Automatic LLM review with possible revision cycles\n\n### 6.2 Version Bumping\n\nConfigure automatic version number incrementing during the commit step:\n\n```yaml\ncommit:\n  version_bumping:\n    enabled: true                  # Enable automatic version bumping\n    file_path: \"pyproject.toml\"    # Path to version file (optional)\n    auto_detect: true              # Auto-detect version file if path not set\n```\n\n**Configuration Options:**\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Description |\n|--------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `enabled` | boolean | `false` | Enable/disable automatic version bumping |\n| `file_path` | string | `null` | Explicit path to version file (relative to project root) |\n| `auto_detect` | boolean | `true` | Automatically detect version file when `file_path` is not set |\n\n**Version File Detection Priority:**\n\nWhen `auto_detect: true`, SE3 searches for version files in this order:\n\n1. `package.json` - Node.js projects (reads `version` field)\n2. `pyproject.toml` - Python projects (reads `project.version`)\n3. `version.py` - Python projects (reads `__version__` variable)\n4. `setup.py` - Python projects (reads `version` keyword argument)\n5. `src/{package}/__init__.py` - Python package init files\n6. `__init__.py` - Root package init files\n\n**Version Bump Rules:**\n\nVersion numbers follow [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/) (SemVer) format: `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`\n\n| Task Type | Bump Type | Version Change | Example |\n|-----------|-----------|----------------|---------|\n| `feature` | minor | Increases MINOR, resets PATCH | `1.2.3` → `1.3.0` |\n| `bugfix` | patch | Increases PATCH | `1.2.3` → `1.2.4` |\n| `breaking` | major | Increases MAJOR, resets MINOR/PATCH | `1.2.3` → `2.0.0` |\n\n**Atomic Commit Guarantee:**\n\nVersion bumping is atomic with git commit:\n- Version file is staged before commit\n- If commit succeeds, version change is preserved\n- If commit fails, version is automatically rolled back to original value\n\n**Example Configuration:**\n\n```yaml\n# Minimal - enable with auto-detection\ncommit:\n  version_bumping:\n    enabled: true\n\n# Explicit - specify version file location\ncommit:\n  version_bumping:\n    enabled: true\n    file_path: \"src/my_package/__init__.py\"\n    auto_detect: false\n\n# Disabled - manual version management\ncommit:\n  version_bumping:\n    enabled: false\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Change Templates\n\n### 7.1 Feature Request\n\n```markdown\n## Summary\nBrief description of the feature.\n\n## Motivation\nWhy is this feature needed?\n\n## Proposed Solution\nHow should this feature work?\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Criterion 1\n- [ ] Criterion 2\n```\n\n### 7.2 Bug Report\n\n```markdown\n## Summary\nBrief description of the bug.\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n1. Step one\n2. Step two\n\n## Expected Behavior\nWhat should happen.\n\n## Actual Behavior\nWhat actually happens.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Related Resources\n\n- <!-- Link to external docs, APIs, etc. -->\n\n---\n\n## Appendix: Spec Metadata\n\n| Property | Value |\n|----------|-------|\n| **Spec ID** | {spec_id} |\n| **Created** | {created_date} |\n| **Modified** | {last_updated} |\n| **Generator** | SE3 Bootstrap v{se3_version} |\n",
